<title>SINGAPORE: RESEARCH ALERT - US funds flow out of Asia - Salomon.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - US funds flow out of Asia - Salomon.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia remains out of favour with U.S. mutual funds, Salomon Brothers said in its latest weekly equity report.</p>
<p>&quot;Asia remains unambigously out of favour with U.S. mutual funds, with year-to-date net outflow of US$1.4 billion, the worst outcome in recent years,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>It said data in recent weeks show no evidence of an upward trend in portfolio capital flows is about to begin anytime soon.</p>
<p>Data showed that for the week to June 18, 1997, net outflow out of the Pacific region was US$131 million.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
